desc: Six Appeal Polysynth (Ultramaster KR-106 port) by chmaha
tags: instrument
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release. Hiding the cursor while dragging faders and knobs needs REAPER 7.83 or later.
about:
  Six-voice 1980s-style polysynth with DCO, OTA ladder filter, BBD chorus and arpeggiator,
  a port of the Ultramaster KR-106 by Karl LaRocca and David Mansfield
  https://github.com/kayrockscreenprinting/ultramaster_kr106 (GPLv3)
  Two engines, each with its own 128-patch factory bank: the 106 engine models the
  firmware (integer envelopes, LFO and filter CV at the 234 Hz main-loop rate) and the
  60 engine models the analog circuits.
  Per-voice component variance, analog noise floor, mains ripple and BBD clock noise,
  hardware voice assignment (Poly 1, Poly 2, Mono), portamento, hold, 6, 8 or 10 voices,
  1x, 2x or 4x filter oversampling, wavetable or PolyBLEP oscillators, and MIDI CC and
  SysEx (IPR/APR) in and out.
  JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code

